# HTML standards

## Markup

- Prefer semantic HTML5 elements over generic wrappers when meaning is clear.
- Keep markup accessible (landmarks, labels, alt text where appropriate).
- Follow current HTML best practices; avoid deprecated attributes and elements.

## File header

At the top of each file, add a file reference:

```html
<!-- --- file: templates/index.html --- -->
```

## Page version (admin cache-bust)

Every operator HTML page must expose a **page version** for deploy verification:

- **Format:** integer only, displayed as `vNN` (e.g. `v24`) — **no** semver on the badge.
- **Placement:** immediately **right of the page title** in the shell header (e.g. `Automation v24`).
- **Visibility:** **admin only** (`isAdmin` / JWT role gate — same as other admin-only chrome).
- **Scope:** **per page** — each HTML entrypoint has its own counter; bump that page’s version when **that** HTML or **its** linked JS changes (shared `wanos-shell.js` / `app.js` bumps every page that includes them — document in commit/chat which pages were bumped).
- **Agent duty:** on every HTML/JS edit that ships to an operator page, **increment** the affected page version(s) and **tell the operator** the latest `vNN` per touched page so they can confirm cache refresh.

Implement via shared shell helper when present (`wanos-shell.js` title block); pages without shell get the same pattern locally.

## Comments

- Update existing comments when markup changes.
- Keep existing comments; remove them only when they are no longer valid.
- Never leave orphaned comments.
- Add comments generously for clarity and programmer context.
